# Shell scripts are LF, always. install.sh is served from raw.githubusercontent
# straight into sh, and a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# whose name ends in a carriage return: "/bin/sh^M", for an error that names a
# path which looks perfectly correct. Scoped to *.sh rather than the whole
# tree, which would renormalise a working copy that is CRLF on purpose.
*.sh text eol=lf
